{
  "id": "COMPOUND:24521 - PROTEIN:6343",
  "verbalization": "Tecleabine is implicated in the regulation of Cyclin-dependent kinase 1/cyclin B through a series of molecular interactions. The evidence suggests that Tecleabine acts as a target of multiple compounds, all of which ultimately influence the activity of Cyclin-dependent kinase 1/cyclin B. Specifically, Tecleabine is linked to HCC1954, which is a target of Phaeocaulisin F, Stemofuran R, and Randainol. These compounds, in turn, target the same downstream pathway, indicating a shared mechanism of action. The presence of multiple overlapping targets and the consistent relationship between Tecleabine and the cyclin-dependent kinase 1/cyclin B suggests a potential role in the regulation of cell cycle progression. The integration of these pathways highlights the importance of cyclin-dependent kinases in cellular processes, and Tecleabine may play a role in modulating their activity.",
